WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:00.963
- Alright.

00:00:00.963 --> 00:00:01.830
Well, Rex, how did this start?

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:04.770
Because you didn't set out to
be popular on Twitter, right?

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.530
- No, you know, I played
basketball for a long time

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:10.299
and this just kind of...

00:00:10.299 --> 00:00:11.400
A couple of years ago,

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.890
I was really frustrated with

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:15.470
the toxic social media

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:17.170
and kinda wanted off.

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:18.890
And I watched so much basketball.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:22.880
I saw this video of a
dolphin swimming out,

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:25.100
a paddle boarder swimming in,

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.270
and a dolphin jumped up

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:28.260
and just hit the guy right in the chest

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.400
and a stupid basketball term.
- I've seen this.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.154
- I said, "That's a
charge, a blocker charge."

00:00:32.154 --> 00:00:32.987
(all laugh)

00:00:32.987 --> 00:00:33.820
Well, I just twitted it out.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:34.653
(woman claps)

00:00:34.653 --> 00:00:36.690
And people thought it was kind of funny.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.443
And then it grew from there.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:40.850
So yeah, I

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:43.210
try to throw in some good feel-good stuff

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:45.270
from time to time to make people laugh.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:49.083
- I mean, that dolphin
video never gets old.

00:00:49.083 --> 00:00:49.916
(man laughs)

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:50.749
- It didn't charge.
- I know (laughs).

00:00:50.749 --> 00:00:53.110
- Because his feet were
planted on the surfboard?

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:54.709
His feet were planted.
- See, see.

00:00:54.709 --> 00:00:55.800
- He couldn't go the
other way 'cause dolphins

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:56.633
don't have feet.
- You know what you're doin'.

00:00:56.633 --> 00:00:57.466
- Oh my God.

00:00:57.466 --> 00:00:58.299
You know, sports ball.
- That's right.

00:00:58.299 --> 00:00:59.650
- I know so much about sports.

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:00.483
People are always like-

00:01:00.483 --> 00:01:01.316
- She does.

00:01:01.316 --> 00:01:02.149
His feet are set.

00:01:02.149 --> 00:01:03.047
Look, that's a charge.

00:01:03.047 --> 00:01:03.880
(woman laughs)

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:04.737
Exactly Eliza called it.

00:01:04.737 --> 00:01:05.570
- I played YMCA basketball.

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:06.530
So I know 'cause

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:07.910
I charged a lot.
- YMCA.

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:09.760
- I got a lot of red flags in lacrosse.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:11.510
So I just know about
the aggressive behavior.

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:12.452
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:12.452 --> 00:01:13.535
I love it, I love that.

00:01:13.535 --> 00:01:14.368
(man laughs)

00:01:14.368 --> 00:01:16.050
Well Rex, it's pretty cool to find a way

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:19.210
to make social media
help your mental state

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:20.440
instead of hurt it

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:21.750
because I'm gonna be honest with you.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.030
I watched "The Social Dilemma."

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:23.863
I don't know if you ever

00:01:23.863 --> 00:01:24.810
if you saw that

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:26.350
but it freaked me out.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:28.300
And I think that, you know,

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:29.721
it is kind of daunting

00:01:29.721 --> 00:01:31.200
the film in general,

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.313
but at the same time,

00:01:32.313 --> 00:01:34.520
I love that you've used it

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:36.170
to help with mental health.

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:38.630
And how have you managed to do that?

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:40.260
- Like I mentioned at the beginning,

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:41.910
I played basketball forever.

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.310
In my last three years of playing,

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:45.600
I had seven orthopedic surgeries.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.540
And right when I finished playing

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.100
I wasn't a drinker, or a smoker, nothing.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.270
My whole career and a
doctor gave me Oxycontin.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:56.290
And that set me on about a 15-year battle

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:57.560
with painkiller addiction.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.423
I had three rehab stints.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:03.110
And so finally about six years ago,

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:05.870
I went to rehab for the third time.

00:02:05.870 --> 00:02:07.342
It took that time.

00:02:07.342 --> 00:02:10.350
I've been off of painkillers
for about six years

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:13.360
and I know life is hard.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:14.810
And you know...

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:16.600
Heck I lived in my car for a little while.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:19.140
I made probably $40
million playing basketball.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:20.270
And since then I've lived

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:22.890
in my car and lived on friend's couches.

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:25.670
So I can't...

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:26.920
I have the greatest debt

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:28.810
of gratitude to so many of my family

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:31.280
and friends who have supported
me through everything.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:33.340
And I think with the Twitter, shoot,

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.100
I'm just happy to be able to bring

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.373
a smile to somebody's face

00:02:37.373 --> 00:02:40.530
and happy that so many people
share their videos with me.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:41.980
None of the content's mine.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:42.870
They send it to me.

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:43.800
I put it out.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:44.633
- Yeah.

00:02:44.633 --> 00:02:46.290
Well you have made me smile a lot.

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:47.140
You're hilarious.

